From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tethering: fall back to modern DNS resolver when dnsmasq is
 unavailable

On GSI builds running on devices with BPF-less kernels, dnsmasq may
fail to start or communicate. The Tethering module hardcodes
usingLegacyDnsProxy=true, which tells netd to rely on dnsmasq for
DNS forwarding. When dnsmasq is not running, nothing listens on port 53
and hotspot clients get ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED.

When the initial tetherStart with legacy DNS proxy fails, retry with
usingLegacyDnsProxy=false. This uses NetworkStackService's built-in
DNS resolver (DnsServerObserver tetherDnsProxy) which does not depend
on dnsmasq at all.

Issue: #14
---
 .../tethering/Tethering.java                 | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java b/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java
+++ b/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java
@@ -2055,14 +2055,29 @@ public class Tethering {
             final String[] dhcpRanges = cfg.useLegacyDhcpServer()
                     ? cfg.legacyDhcpRanges : new String[0];
             try {
                 NetdUtils.tetherStart(mNetd, true /** usingLegacyDnsProxy */, dhcpRanges);
             } catch (RemoteException | ServiceSpecificException e) {
                 try {
                     // Stop and retry.
                     mNetd.tetherStop();
-                    NetdUtils.tetherStart(mNetd, true /** usingLegacyDnsProxy */, dhcpRanges);
+                    // dnsmasq may have failed on BPF-less kernels. Retry
+                    // without the legacy DNS proxy so that NetworkStackService
+                    // provides its own DNS resolver (tetherDnsProxy) instead.
+                    mLog.log("Legacy DNS proxy (dnsmasq) start failed, "
+                            + "retrying with modern DNS resolver");
+                    NetdUtils.tetherStart(mNetd, false /** usingLegacyDnsProxy */, dhcpRanges);
                 } catch (RemoteException | ServiceSpecificException ee) {
                     mLog.e(ee);
                     transitionTo(mStartTetheringErrorState);
                     return false;
                 }
             }
             mLog.log("SET main tether settings: ON");

-- 
